    "updated_at": "2026-11-19T10:52:36Z",
    "body": "> I think if we store the inherited namespace (including \"`html`\") on the `template` element and force it when serializing (and remove any developer-set attribute of that name first) we are good.\n\nDoes it get reflected in getAttribute or contentNamespace getter?\n\nThis is not just about serializing, it's about how the template behaves post-parsing eg when it gets moved around and used as a fragment parser context.\n\n\n> \n> We also have to account for it with fragment parsing.\n> \n> Not inheriting would give a bad experience for SVG and MathML.\n\nIt just means templates are html by default unless given an explicit attribute. \n\n> \n> I'm not entirely convinced yet that `type` is the name we want here. I would prefer `contentnamespace`. And have the `contentNamespace` IDL attribute always return the qualified namespace (make it return the internal state, where we just use the actual namespace).\n\nThat's what I use in the PR, I agree.\n\n",
