    "body": "Here's the model I think we should go with, taking the feedback above into account:\n\n- A `template` element has a content namespace (HTML, SVG, or MathML) that sticks with the element:\n  - The HTML parser sets it from the `contentnamespace` attribute if that has a valid value. Otherwise it inherits from the adjusted current node: SVG or MathML inside `svg`/`math`, HTML at integration points, the outer template's namespace for a nested template, and HTML everywhere else.\n  - The XML parser does the same, with the parent in place of the adjusted current node, and HTML when there's no HTML, SVG, or MathML parent.\n  - `createElement()` gives HTML. Cloning copies it.\n- The `contentnamespace` attribute is only looked at when parsing, like `shadowrootmode`. Changing or removing it later does nothing, so a sanitizer that strips unknown attributes can't change the namespace of contents it has already checked.\n- `contentNamespace` gets and sets the content namespace as a namespace URL, and throws for anything other than the HTML, SVG, or MathML namespace. It doesn't reflect the attribute; `getAttribute()` returns whatever the author wrote. Code that only uses `setAttribute()` won't work, and I think that's fine.\n- Fragment parsing with a template as context uses its content namespace. So moving a template doesn't change how markup parses in it, and `t.innerHTML = t.innerHTML` is stable (unless you changed `contentNamespace` in between).\n- The serializer always emits `contentnamespace` with the content namespace (including `html`) as the first attribute, and skips the element's own `contentnamespace` attribute. (I guess I'm willing to entertain a robust alternative, but it gets complex fast and that doesn't seem worth it for serialization.)\n- `shadowrootmode` only takes precedence when a shadow root is actually attached. Otherwise the content namespace applies, which covers zcorpan's case of a `<template shadowrootmode>` that didn't get attached.\n- A `<template for>` without a valid `contentnamespace` that successfully patches inherits from the patch target instead.\n- `<template/>` in SVG and MathML keeps working as it does today. It just creates an empty HTML template now.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
