    "body": "> Here's the model I think we should go with, taking the feedback above into account:\n\nThis is all fine with me % comnent \n\n> * A `<template for>` without a valid `contentnamespace` that successfully patches inherits from the patch target instead.\n\nDoes this allow patching with SVG into HTML? Maybe `<template for>` should always take the patching target and ignore the attribute?\n\nPerhaps a better alternative is to error the patch if it has an explicit `contentnamespace` attribute that doesn't match the target.\n",
